course: dictionary
lesson: 14712
title: Proclamation: a public announcement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A proclamation is an official public announcement. It is a message made loudly and clearly so that everyone can hear it. Kings, queens, presidents and governments make proclamations.
explain: «The king's proclamation was read out in the town square.» The words official and public are the clues. This is a formal message for everyone, not a private chat. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The king's official announcement was read out in the town square" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: The word can also mean a clear, strong public statement of a belief or idea. «Her proclamation that everyone deserves a fair chance rang out across the hall.» Here Maya is not making an official law. She is boldly saying what she believes.
explain: History is full of proclamations. In 1863 Abraham Lincoln issued the Emancipation Proclamation, which declared that enslaved people in the states fighting against the United States were free. When you meet a word like this in a history book, check the context first, then use a dictionary if you are still unsure.
fact: A proclamation is an official public announcement.
fact: «Proclamation» can mean a clear, strong public statement of a belief or idea.
fact: Royal proclamations are announcements made by a king or queen.
fact: The Emancipation Proclamation was issued by Abraham Lincoln in 1863.
fact: The Proclamation of the Irish Republic was read out in Dublin in 1916.
exercise: «The king's proclamation was read out in the town square.» What is a proclamation? | A private letter to one person | *An official public announcement | A type of castle wall | A quiet note passed between friends
exercise: In the story, a herald reads out the king's proclamation. What does the herald do? | Writes a secret note to the king | *Reads the official message aloud to the people | Hides the message in a box | Sells food in the market
exercise: «Her proclamation that everyone deserves a fair chance rang out across the hall.» Find and copy one word that means a strong, clear public statement. | *proclamation | everyone | chance | hall
test: «The Emancipation Proclamation was issued by Abraham Lincoln in 1863.» What kind of word is proclamation here? | *A noun naming an official announcement | A name for a country | An adjective meaning very small | A verb meaning to hide something
test: Ella says, «A proclamation is just a normal chat between two friends.» Is she right? | Yes, it is a private talk | *No, it is official and meant for everyone to hear | No, it is a public announcement or statement | Yes, if it is said quietly
exam: Read: «The mayor's proclamation said the school would close early for the flood.» What does proclamation mean, and which clue in the sentence tells you? | *An official public announcement, because the mayor is in charge and it reaches everyone | A private note, because the school closes | A ball game, because it is about playing | A song, because it is said aloud
